<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The lower layer of the adaptive icon (Android 8+).

  @capacitor/assets writes #FFFFFF here by default, which is wrong for this
  icon: the foreground layer is the brand rounded square inset to the 66% safe
  zone, so a white background shows as a pale ring around it under the
  launcher's circle / squircle mask. Painting the background the same brand
  violet makes the whole tile one solid colour whatever mask the device applies.

  The value is the "brand" accent token from web/src/index.css. Re-running
  `npm run brand` at the repo root (or the `assets:gen` script inside web/)
  resets this file and mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher*.xml back to the white
  default — reapply both together.

  NOTE: never write two consecutive hyphens anywhere in this comment. XML
  forbids them inside a comment, and aapt fails :app:mergeDebugResources with
  «The string is not permitted within comments». That is why the CSS custom
  property and the npm flag are described in prose instead of quoted verbatim.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#7C5CFF</color>
</resources>
